{"step_index":2517,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:09:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T15:09:12+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T15:09:13+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/search.py`\nTotal Lines: 61\nTotal Bytes: 2188\nShowing lines 1 to 61\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import numpy as np\n2: from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n3: from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n4: import re\n5: \n6: def normalize_for_search(text: str) -> str:\n7:     \"\"\"Basic normalization for character n-gram search.\"\"\"\n8:     if not text:\n9:         return \"\"\n10:     text = str(text).lower()\n11:     text = re.sub(r'[\\u064B-\\u065F\\u0670]', '', text) # Remove Arabic diacritics\n12:     text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', ' ', text) # Replace punctuation with spaces\n13:     text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n14:     return text\n15: \n16: class FastCandidateFinder:\n17:     def __init__(self):\n18:         # Use Character N-Grams (2 to 4 chars) to catch slight misspellings automatically\n19:         self.vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(analyzer='char_wb', ngram_range=(2, 4))\n20:         self.corpus = []\n21:         self.original_names = []\n22:         self.ids = []\n23:         self.matrix = None\n24: \n25:     def fit(self, warehouse_items: list[dict]):\n26:         \"\"\"\n27:         warehouse_items: list of dicts with 'id' and 'name'\n28:         \"\"\"\n29:         self.ids = [item[\"id\"] for item in warehouse_items]\n30:         self.original_names = [item[\"name\"] for item in warehouse_items]\n31:         self.corpus = [normalize_for_search(name) for name in self.original_names]\n32:         \n33:         if self.corpus:\n34:             self.matrix = self.vectorizer.fit_transform(self.corpus)\n35: \n36:     def search(self, query: str, top_k: int = 5) -> list[dict]:\n37:         \"\"\"Returns the top_k most similar items from the warehouse.\"\"\"\n38:         if not self.corpus:\n39:             return []\n40:             \n41:         q_norm = normalize_for_search(query)\n42:         if not q_norm:\n43:             return []\n44:             \n45:         q_vec = self.vectorizer.transform([q_norm])\n46:         sims = cosine_similarity(q_vec, self.matrix).flatten()\n47:         \n48:         # Get top K indices\n49:         top_indices = np.argsort(sims)[-top_k:][::-1]\n50:         \n51:         results = []\n52:         for idx in top_indices:\n53:             score = float(sims[idx])\n54:             if score > 0.1:  # Ignore completely unrelated items\n55:                 results.append({\n56:                     \"id\": self.ids[idx],\n57:                     \"name\": self.original_names[idx],\n58:                     \"score\": score\n59:                 })\n60:         return results\n61: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":2518,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:09:13Z","thinking":"Analyzing the `normalize_for_search` function, the agent is implementing specific Arabic text normalization rules. This includes character mapping for alef variations, ya variants, teh marbuta, numerals, and removal of tatweel and diacritics, along with punctuation to spaces. The agent aims to preserve critical words and numbers as instructed, implying a focus on maintaining semantic content for the language model.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"& \"D:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe\" -c \"\nimport re\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n\ndef norm(text):\n    text = str(text).lower()\n    text = re.sub(r'[\\u064B-\\u065F\\u0670\\u0640]', '', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'[أإآ]', 'ا', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'ة', 'ه', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'ى', 'ي', text)\n    # Eastern Arabic to Western digits\n    for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩', '0123456789'):\n        text = text.replace(e, w)\n    text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', ' ', text)\n    return re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n\nv = TfidfVectorizer(analyzer='char_wb', ngram_range=(2, 4))\ncorp = [norm('بانادول اكسترا 48 قرص-96ب'), norm('كليكسان 40مجم-84'), norm('ايزوتريتينوين 20م جديد -50')]\nmat = v.fit_transform(corp)\n\nq = norm('بنادول اكسترا احمر 24قرص س ج')\nsims = cosine_similarity(v.transform([q]), mat)[0]\nprint('Panadol sim:', sims[0])\n\"","Cwd":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing improved normalization on Panadol","toolSummary":"Test improved normalization"}}]}
